Paper: "PointMamba: A Simple State Space Model for Point Cloud Analysis",
       NeurIPS 2024

This is a derivative work adapted for the LIDARLearn library.
Changes from the original:
  - Integrated into the LIDARLearn model registry and config system;
    classes renamed PointMambaScan -> PointMamba and
    Point_MAE_Mamba_serializationV2 -> PointMamba_Pretrain
    (parameter names unchanged, so the released checkpoints load as-is)
  - PointMamba uses the BasePointCloudModel base class (loss/accuracy)
  - Uses LIDARLearn's KNN, FPS, Chamfer distance and checkpoint loader
    instead of knn_cuda and the bundled extensions
  - Mamba blocks taken from the official mamba-ssm package instead of the
    vendored copy; RMSNorm imported from mamba_ssm.ops.triton.layer_norm
  - load_model_from_ckpt returns the missing/unexpected keys
  - Removed unused code (Mlp block, commented-out alternatives)

mamba_blocks.py keeps the block design of Mamba
(Copyright (c) 2023, Tri Dao, Albert Gu; Apache-2.0).

models/pointmamba/serialization.py and models/pointmamba/hilbert.py come from
Pointcept (https://github.com/Pointcept/Pointcept, MIT licence, see
LICENSE-Pointcept) via the PointMamba repository and are unchanged apart from
their header. hilbert.py is modified from numpy-hilbert-curve
(https://github.com/PrincetonLIPS/numpy-hilbert-curve, MIT licence, see
LICENSE-numpy-hilbert-curve).

Also derived from the PointMamba repository (and, through it, Point-BERT /
Point-MAE):
  - datasets/ScanObjectNNDataset.py: one shared base class for the OBJ-BG /
    OBJ-ONLY and PB-T50-RS loaders, official class names added, clear error
    when the h5 files are missing
  - datasets/augmentation.py RandomYRotate ('y_rotate'): same rotation as
    PointcloudRotate, used for PointMamba pretraining and ScanObjectNN
